-- title:
--   Additivity of the supersingular Hecke operator T_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and an algebraically closed field $K$ of characteristic $p$ with decidable equality, a level $N \ne 0$ whose image in $K$ is nonzero, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \ne p$; fix an integer weight $k$. The index type $\mathrm{SSIndex}$ consists of those places $x$ of the function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ (the intermediate field of the Laurent series over $K$ generated by $jq$ and $jq_N$) that lie in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,p\,N\,K$ and satisfy $2 \le k$, $2 \mid k$, $\mathrm{placeWidth}\,N\,x \mid k/2$ and $5 \le p$, and the carrier $\mathrm{SSCarrier}$ is the space of all $K$-valued functions on this index type, with pointwise addition. The assertion is that for all $v, w$ in this carrier, $$\mathrm{ssHeckeFun}\,(v+w) = \mathrm{ssHeckeFun}\,v + \mathrm{ssHeckeFun}\,w,$$ where $\mathrm{ssHeckeFun}$ sends $v$ to the function whose value at $x$ is $\ell^{k/2-1}$ times the leading coefficient $\mathrm{lead}$ at $x$, in the normalisation given by $\mathrm{poleOrder}$, of the trace from $\mathrm{charLDegeneracyRoof}\,K\,N\,\ell$ down to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,K\,N$ along $\mathrm{heckeAlphaC}$ of $\mathrm{heckeBetaC}(\mathrm{liftFun}\,v)$ multiplied by $\mathrm{heckeMultiplier}^{(k/2)_+}$, the lift $\mathrm{liftFun}\,v$ being a choice of function in the field with prescribed pole bounds at the supersingular places and prescribed leading coefficients $v$.
--
--   This is the additivity half of the statement that the $\ell$-th Hecke operator on weight-$k$ supersingular values is $K$-linear, the point being that the value does not depend on the chosen lift of the prescribed leading coefficients. It is used, together with the homogeneity statement, in assembling the supersingular datum over an algebraically closed field and in the windowing comparison [`ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window`](thm.html#ModularCurve.SSHeckeV2.ssHeckeFun_window).
